1
00:00:01,208 --> 00:00:04,458
[ethereal music playing]

2
00:00:06,208 --> 00:00:08,291
[♪♪♪]

3
00:00:08,291 --> 00:00:10,958
For the glory of the Sources.

4
00:00:11,791 --> 00:00:13,666
[bushes rustling]

5
00:00:16,708 --> 00:00:18,500
Greetings, traveler.

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,708
[Chief Loyalist] This is it?

7
00:00:19,708 --> 00:00:21,750
The Shrine of the Seven Sources?

8
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:22,916
Yes.

9
00:00:22,916 --> 00:00:24,583
Have you come to pay homage

10
00:00:24,583 --> 00:00:26,125
to our humble shrine?

11
00:00:26,125 --> 00:00:28,041
[Chief Loyalist]
"Humble" is right.

12
00:00:28,041 --> 00:00:30,375
I expected something
a little more impressive.

13
00:00:30,375 --> 00:00:32,250
Praise of the Source Dragons

14
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:35,250
has little to do
with outward displays...

15
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:38,500
only inner devotion.

16
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:41,125
[Chief Loyalist]
How very "enlightened" of you.

17
00:00:41,125 --> 00:00:42,583
So, each column
channels the presence

18
00:00:42,583 --> 00:00:44,416
of the power
of one of the Source Dragons?

19
00:00:44,416 --> 00:00:46,750
You've done your research.

20
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:50,416
As long as a Dragon's energy
flows through the lands,

21
00:00:50,416 --> 00:00:53,541
its column will glow forth
as a tribute.

22
00:00:53,541 --> 00:00:54,541
Sadly,

23
00:00:54,541 --> 00:00:56,875
one of the Source Dragons
has passed,

24
00:00:56,875 --> 00:01:00,250
but one day,
when the cycle renews, all--

25
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,500
[Chief Loyalist] Yes, yes,
yes, "Praise the Sources"

26
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:02,500
or whatever,

27
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:05,291
but have you observed
any fluctuations

28
00:01:05,291 --> 00:01:06,458
or anomalies

29
00:01:06,458 --> 00:01:08,583
in the power distribution recently?

30
00:01:08,583 --> 00:01:09,750
Uh...

31
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:11,291
I'm... I'm sorry,

32
00:01:11,291 --> 00:01:14,875
I... I don't
understand the question.

33
00:01:14,875 --> 00:01:16,958
[Chief Loyalist]
I'm looking for any indication

34
00:01:16,958 --> 00:01:18,708
of--
-[rumbling]

35
00:01:18,708 --> 00:01:19,666
--of that!

36
00:01:19,666 --> 00:01:20,833
[gasping in shock]

37
00:01:20,833 --> 00:01:24,000
[Chief Loyalist]
Ha! Just as I hypothesized.

38
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,125
Source withdrawal.

39
00:01:26,125 --> 00:01:30,250
I'm... I'm sure this outage
is only temporary.

40
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:33,750
Besides, we still have
five mighty Sources--

41
00:01:35,333 --> 00:01:36,250
[gasping]

42
00:01:36,250 --> 00:01:38,583
No cause for alarm.

43
00:01:38,583 --> 00:01:39,666
There are still a majority--

44
00:01:40,625 --> 00:01:41,750
[gasping in horror]

45
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:43,500
[crackling and rumbling]

46
00:01:44,958 --> 00:01:46,625
[Acolytes gasping]

47
00:01:46,625 --> 00:01:48,458
[Acolyte] A majority of Sources

48
00:01:48,458 --> 00:01:50,958
have removed their power
from the lands?

49
00:01:50,958 --> 00:01:55,958
Great Dragons, why have you
forsaken us mortals?

50
00:01:58,916 --> 00:02:00,333
[gasping]

51
00:02:04,041 --> 00:02:05,416
[bubbling]

52
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:14,250
[snarling]

53
00:02:16,541 --> 00:02:18,541
[roaring]

54
00:02:18,541 --> 00:02:19,416
[Acolytes screaming]

55
00:02:19,416 --> 00:02:20,333
[monsters roaring]

56
00:02:21,958 --> 00:02:23,583
[roaring]

57
00:02:23,583 --> 00:02:25,083
[acid hissing]

58
00:02:31,458 --> 00:02:32,833
[screaming]

59
00:02:32,833 --> 00:02:34,166
[Chief Loyalist] As predicted,

60
00:02:34,166 --> 00:02:36,791
the manifestations
have already begun.

61
00:02:36,791 --> 00:02:40,708
The foolish Ninja have played
right into our hands.

62
00:02:40,708 --> 00:02:44,583
The quest for Desolation
begins now.

63
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:47,250
[screaming]

64
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:49,375
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

65
00:02:49,375 --> 00:02:50,750
♪ So much to see ♪

66
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:54,208
♪ Jump up, kick back
whip around and spin ♪

67
00:02:54,208 --> 00:02:55,250
♪ Together we will rise ♪

68
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:56,916
♪ Whip around and spin ♪

69
00:02:56,916 --> 00:02:58,208
♪ Together we will rise ♪

70
00:02:58,208 --> 00:03:01,458
♪ For what's right ♪

71
00:03:03,125 --> 00:03:05,583
[Lloyd]
He was called "ThunderFang,

72
00:03:05,583 --> 00:03:07,500
the Shatter Dragon of Chaos."

73
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:09,833
[Arin]
Scary name, scary dragon.

74
00:03:09,833 --> 00:03:11,708
Also long name, long dragon.

75
00:03:11,708 --> 00:03:12,958
Only way to beat him?

76
00:03:12,958 --> 00:03:15,291
Summon ThunderFang's
old nemesis,

77
00:03:15,291 --> 00:03:17,541
the Arc Dragon of Focus.

78
00:03:17,541 --> 00:03:21,041
[Lloyd] Classic matchup,
Chaos versus Focus,

79
00:03:21,041 --> 00:03:22,541
but ThunderFang
was so powered up,

80
00:03:22,541 --> 00:03:24,916
the Focus Dragon
couldn't do it alone.

81
00:03:24,916 --> 00:03:26,625
[Arin]
So we helped guide them.

82
00:03:26,625 --> 00:03:29,000
I know it sounds unbelievable,

83
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,291
but our minds were, like,
sharing a dragon's brain!

84
00:03:32,291 --> 00:03:33,583
[Lloyd]
With the Focus Dragon's help,

85
00:03:33,583 --> 00:03:36,250
we beat ThunderFang for good.

86
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:37,583
World saved!

87
00:03:37,583 --> 00:03:39,000
[Arin]
But some of the Source Dragons

88
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,416
might not be happy with us

89
00:03:40,416 --> 00:03:42,958
for summoning that Arc Dragon
without their permission.

90
00:03:42,958 --> 00:03:45,083
[Lloyd] So, we were heading
back to Ninjago

91
00:03:45,083 --> 00:03:47,875
when I felt something weird
going on with my powers.

92
00:03:47,875 --> 00:03:49,875
Then we went though
the portal gate--

93
00:03:49,875 --> 00:03:51,625
And it spat us out here.

94
00:03:51,625 --> 00:03:53,416
Wherever "here" is,

95
00:03:53,416 --> 00:03:55,208
it's obviously not home,

96
00:03:55,208 --> 00:03:57,083
so we tried to go back
through the portal--

97
00:03:57,083 --> 00:03:58,291
And it wouldn't work.

98
00:03:58,291 --> 00:03:59,625
Totally inactive,

99
00:03:59,625 --> 00:04:02,000
but how are you here?

100
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,541
Basically same?

101
00:04:03,541 --> 00:04:07,458
Minus the dragon
mind-brain thing.

102
00:04:07,458 --> 00:04:08,791
I was in the Cloud Kingdom,

103
00:04:08,791 --> 00:04:10,916
felt my Powers going weird.

104
00:04:10,916 --> 00:04:13,583
I wanted to ask
you Ninja about it, but...

105
00:04:13,583 --> 00:04:17,375
when I went through the gate,
it sent me here.

106
00:04:17,375 --> 00:04:19,750
Sorry you got stranded too,

107
00:04:19,750 --> 00:04:22,083
but it's nice to see you again.

108
00:04:23,416 --> 00:04:26,416
So you have no idea
what happened?

109
00:04:26,416 --> 00:04:29,000
To our powers
or the Portal Gates?

110
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,583
[Lloyd] No idea.

111
00:04:30,583 --> 00:04:31,833
Let's check out
the neighborhood.

112
00:04:31,833 --> 00:04:32,833
It might have some answers.

113
00:04:39,458 --> 00:04:41,416
[Arin] Wow...

114
00:04:41,416 --> 00:04:44,250
It's beautiful.

115
00:04:45,041 --> 00:04:48,625
You Cloud Monks record stuff
about all the lands, right?

116
00:04:48,625 --> 00:04:50,625
Any idea where we are?

117
00:04:50,625 --> 00:04:53,750
My focus is the Wyldness's
late medieval period.

118
00:04:53,750 --> 00:04:57,416
I've never seen anything
quite like this place.

119
00:04:57,416 --> 00:04:59,000
Me neither.

120
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:00,250
Hopefully the other Ninja

121
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:03,333
aren't having
the same problems we are.

122
00:05:05,958 --> 00:05:07,500
[Nya] This is not Ninjago.

123
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:09,625
We needed to get back
to Ninjago.

124
00:05:09,625 --> 00:05:12,208
Why is the Portal Gate
malfunctioning?

125
00:05:12,208 --> 00:05:13,416
[Kai] What's also weird?

126
00:05:13,416 --> 00:05:15,750
When we left Mysterium,
it was day.

127
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:17,708
Now it's
the middle of the night.

128
00:05:17,708 --> 00:05:19,166
[Jay] A cloudy night.

129
00:05:19,166 --> 00:05:21,458
No moons, no stars.

130
00:05:26,708 --> 00:05:27,958
[Kai] A fireball
should light things up.

131
00:05:27,958 --> 00:05:29,875
[spluttering]

132
00:05:29,875 --> 00:05:31,375
Oh, yeah, guess what.

133
00:05:31,375 --> 00:05:33,666
Elemental Powers
are also on the fritz.

134
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:34,916
Hold on, let me try this.

135
00:05:34,916 --> 00:05:36,416
H'yah!

136
00:05:36,416 --> 00:05:38,958
[groaning]

137
00:05:39,041 --> 00:05:40,791
[laughing]

138
00:05:40,791 --> 00:05:42,291
I was feeling bummed

139
00:05:42,291 --> 00:05:44,375
about our powers
not working right,

140
00:05:44,375 --> 00:05:45,750
but that made me feel
a little better.

141
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:47,375
I'll remember this

142
00:05:47,375 --> 00:05:48,625
when you end up
zapping yourself

143
00:05:48,625 --> 00:05:50,166
with a giant lightning storm.

144
00:05:50,166 --> 00:05:53,166
Nya, can't you get
the Portal Gate going again?

145
00:05:53,166 --> 00:05:54,916
[Nya] Get it going how?

146
00:05:54,916 --> 00:05:56,166
It's powered down.

147
00:05:56,166 --> 00:05:57,166
We don't even know

148
00:05:57,166 --> 00:05:58,750
how or why it spat us out here.

149
00:05:59,291 --> 00:06:00,458
Um...

150
00:06:00,458 --> 00:06:02,583
Take us to Ninjago!

151
00:06:04,125 --> 00:06:06,333
See? Nothing.

152
00:06:06,333 --> 00:06:07,791
Looks like we have to
find another way

153
00:06:07,791 --> 00:06:09,625
back to Ninjago.

154
00:06:09,625 --> 00:06:11,166
I say we wait till sun-up

155
00:06:11,166 --> 00:06:12,625
so we can see where we are,

156
00:06:12,625 --> 00:06:14,041
then take it from there.

157
00:06:14,041 --> 00:06:16,125
[smashing]

158
00:06:17,458 --> 00:06:19,708
Hey, Kai, we're gonna need
a campfire.

159
00:06:19,708 --> 00:06:21,666
Think you could, um...

160
00:06:21,666 --> 00:06:22,916
[scoffing] Of course I can.

161
00:06:22,916 --> 00:06:25,125
Hah! H'yah!

162
00:06:25,125 --> 00:06:26,541
You set him up for that
on purpose,

163
00:06:26,541 --> 00:06:27,750
didn't you?
-[shrugging] Hmm.

164
00:06:27,750 --> 00:06:30,791
[Sora] Portal Gates are usually
in monasteries,

165
00:06:30,791 --> 00:06:33,500
and I don't see a monastery
around here,

166
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,791
unless--

167
00:06:35,791 --> 00:06:37,833
[Wyldfyre grunting]
Come on, come on!

168
00:06:37,833 --> 00:06:40,541
If I can't blast fireballs,
who even am I?

169
00:06:40,541 --> 00:06:41,541
[Frak] Wait...

170
00:06:41,541 --> 00:06:42,583
Feel that?

171
00:06:42,583 --> 00:06:43,666
Like a little tremor?

172
00:06:43,666 --> 00:06:44,958
You felt that, right?

173
00:06:44,958 --> 00:06:46,625
[Riyu grumbling negatively]

174
00:06:46,625 --> 00:06:48,125
[groaning] You're right.

175
00:06:48,125 --> 00:06:49,416
Who am I kidding?

176
00:06:49,416 --> 00:06:50,750
There was no tremor!

177
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:53,333
If I can't quake, what'll I do?

178
00:06:53,333 --> 00:06:54,666
What am I even good for?

179
00:06:54,666 --> 00:06:56,958
Your powers aren't
what give you your worth.

180
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,083
Of course they are!

181
00:06:58,083 --> 00:07:00,375
Yeah, what are you
talking about, Sora?

182
00:07:00,375 --> 00:07:01,875
Please freak out like us.

183
00:07:01,875 --> 00:07:03,041
I was solving problems

184
00:07:03,041 --> 00:07:05,791
long before I had
an Elemental Power.

185
00:07:05,791 --> 00:07:08,083
And this is a problem.

186
00:07:08,083 --> 00:07:09,708
I mean,
the portal gate spit us out

187
00:07:09,708 --> 00:07:11,916
in some random, unknown spot?

188
00:07:11,916 --> 00:07:12,750
Why?

189
00:07:12,750 --> 00:07:14,250
And our powers.

190
00:07:14,250 --> 00:07:16,416
Don't forget
our powers problem.

191
00:07:16,416 --> 00:07:18,083
Kai will know what's going on.

192
00:07:18,083 --> 00:07:20,208
We need to get back to Ninjago.

193
00:07:20,208 --> 00:07:21,208
Yeah,

194
00:07:21,208 --> 00:07:23,041
but without a working
Portal Gate,

195
00:07:23,041 --> 00:07:24,541
looks like we're walking.

196
00:07:24,541 --> 00:07:27,333
And in which direction?

197
00:07:27,333 --> 00:07:28,791
And...

198
00:07:28,791 --> 00:07:30,000
Wait.

199
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:34,166
It's dawn everywhere.

200
00:07:35,541 --> 00:07:38,166
So, this kinda makes
knowing what direction to go

201
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:40,541
a little hard, right?

202
00:07:40,541 --> 00:07:42,625
A little.

203
00:07:43,791 --> 00:07:45,708
[stomach grumbling]

204
00:07:45,708 --> 00:07:47,958
I can hear
your stomachs growling.

205
00:07:47,958 --> 00:07:50,541
I've got these wafers left.

206
00:07:50,541 --> 00:07:52,458
It wasn't my stomach, for once.

207
00:07:52,458 --> 00:07:53,708
Not me either.

208
00:07:53,708 --> 00:07:56,083
Plus, I'd rather starve
than eat those.

209
00:07:57,791 --> 00:08:00,250
What's with
the miserable faces?

210
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:01,666
It's not like this is
the first time

211
00:08:01,666 --> 00:08:04,666
we've been stuck
in some unknown place.

212
00:08:04,666 --> 00:08:06,333
Remember the Never-Realm?

213
00:08:06,333 --> 00:08:09,708
Or in Prime Empire, when...

214
00:08:09,708 --> 00:08:11,125
Oh...

215
00:08:11,125 --> 00:08:12,625
right.

216
00:08:12,625 --> 00:08:15,000
You don't remember any of that.

217
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:18,208
No, I don't.

218
00:08:18,208 --> 00:08:20,666
Back in the City of Temples,

219
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:22,458
do you know why I left?

220
00:08:22,458 --> 00:08:23,875
We hadn't paid you yet?

221
00:08:23,875 --> 00:08:24,875
No!

222
00:08:25,916 --> 00:08:27,916
I was watching you all,

223
00:08:27,916 --> 00:08:29,583
the way you worked together,

224
00:08:29,583 --> 00:08:31,625
more like a family
than a team...

225
00:08:31,625 --> 00:08:34,166
a family I had no memory of,

226
00:08:34,166 --> 00:08:37,958
and that made me feel
more lonely than I'd ever felt.

227
00:08:39,625 --> 00:08:41,958
I had to get away.

228
00:08:43,375 --> 00:08:44,791
But as soon as I was gone,

229
00:08:44,791 --> 00:08:46,208
I regretted it.

230
00:08:46,208 --> 00:08:49,875
especially after
what you said to me, Nya.

231
00:08:49,875 --> 00:08:53,250
I don't know if you'll ever
get those memories back, Jay,

232
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:54,958
but we're together now.

233
00:08:54,958 --> 00:08:57,500
We can build new memories.

234
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:59,000
But that's just it.

235
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,166
The more time I spend with you,
I realize...

236
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:04,333
I need more than new memories.

237
00:09:04,333 --> 00:09:07,625
I need to remember
the first time we met.

238
00:09:07,625 --> 00:09:09,791
The first time we danced.

239
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:15,500
The first time
I made you smile.

240
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:18,208
Those memories
can't be gone forever.

241
00:09:18,208 --> 00:09:20,250
They have to be somewhere
in your mind.

242
00:09:20,250 --> 00:09:23,541
We just have to find a way
to bring them back.

243
00:09:28,916 --> 00:09:31,250
[bird tweeting]

244
00:09:31,250 --> 00:09:32,500
[♪♪♪]

245
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:34,125
[birds chirping, music playing]

246
00:09:36,166 --> 00:09:38,916
[♪♪♪]

247
00:09:42,666 --> 00:09:44,625
[low rumbling]

248
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:47,166
Zane, are you okay?

249
00:09:47,166 --> 00:09:49,000
I'm not sure, Pixal.

250
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,625
I feel... off.

251
00:09:52,583 --> 00:09:55,208
My powers... are gone?

252
00:09:55,208 --> 00:09:57,250
[spluttering]

253
00:09:57,250 --> 00:09:58,541
[yelping] Ah!

254
00:09:58,541 --> 00:09:59,916
[birds retreating,
chirping in alarm]

255
00:09:59,916 --> 00:10:01,666
Something's very wrong.

256
00:10:01,666 --> 00:10:03,583
I've gotta find the other Ninja.

257
00:10:04,583 --> 00:10:06,291
There are plenty
of worse places

258
00:10:06,291 --> 00:10:07,958
to get stranded, I guess,

259
00:10:07,958 --> 00:10:09,791
and after everything
we've been through,

260
00:10:09,791 --> 00:10:11,666
I'm cool with a little peace.

261
00:10:11,666 --> 00:10:14,166
Yeah, this is
the exact opposite

262
00:10:14,166 --> 00:10:15,916
of fighting undead dragons.

263
00:10:15,916 --> 00:10:18,166
Or crawling through
the Underworld.

264
00:10:18,166 --> 00:10:19,833
You went to the Underworld?

265
00:10:19,833 --> 00:10:22,208
I feel like
Ras dragged me everywhere.

266
00:10:22,208 --> 00:10:23,416
Ras?

267
00:10:23,416 --> 00:10:25,708
That tiger guy that attacked
the Cloud Kingdom?

268
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:26,583
Who talks all--

269
00:10:26,583 --> 00:10:29,000
"No one will stop me,

270
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:32,666
I'm so mean, roar-roar"
and stuff?

271
00:10:32,666 --> 00:10:33,958
[chuckling] Yeah.

272
00:10:33,958 --> 00:10:36,541
A lot's happened since we last
hung out, Euphrasia.

273
00:10:36,541 --> 00:10:39,208
I even stupidly
left the Ninja team.

274
00:10:39,208 --> 00:10:41,791
You did what you thought
you needed to do, Arin.

275
00:10:41,791 --> 00:10:44,500
I was so caught up
in other problems,

276
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:46,333
I should have seen
what you were going through.

277
00:10:46,333 --> 00:10:48,625
You have
so many responsibilities,

278
00:10:48,625 --> 00:10:50,333
I don't blame you
for that, Lloyd.

279
00:10:50,333 --> 00:10:53,083
I should have been the one
to teach you proper Spinjitzu.

280
00:10:53,083 --> 00:10:55,375
Ras showed me
how to do that, yes,

281
00:10:55,375 --> 00:10:58,416
but I'm not sure
it was the best way.

282
00:10:58,416 --> 00:11:01,166
He... exploited my anger.

283
00:11:01,166 --> 00:11:04,000
I can't believe you have
an angry bone in your body.

284
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,083
I was mad at Master Wu
for causing the Merge.

285
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:09,333
I blamed him for the death
of my parents,

286
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:11,666
but my parents were still alive.

287
00:11:11,666 --> 00:11:14,083
I should never
have trusted Ras.

288
00:11:14,083 --> 00:11:16,666
Master Wu caused the Merge?

289
00:11:16,666 --> 00:11:17,708
Why?

290
00:11:17,708 --> 00:11:19,291
You have no idea

291
00:11:19,291 --> 00:11:22,166
how badly I wish I knew
the answer to that question.

292
00:11:23,375 --> 00:11:24,750
[wind gusting, faint whispering]

293
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:26,500
You hear that?

294
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:27,500
Is someone there?

295
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,208
[disembodied whispering]

296
00:11:32,375 --> 00:11:34,458
[disembodied whispering]

297
00:11:34,458 --> 00:11:35,375
Odd.

298
00:11:35,375 --> 00:11:37,750
[wind gusting]

299
00:11:38,666 --> 00:11:39,958
[whispers swirling]

300
00:11:39,958 --> 00:11:43,083
Okay, a little bit creepy.

301
00:11:43,083 --> 00:11:46,416
Maybe a lot a bit creepy.

302
00:11:46,416 --> 00:11:50,000
[woodland birds,
disembodied whispering]

303
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,166
Is someone following us?

304
00:11:52,166 --> 00:11:54,375
We don't even know
if anyone lives here.

305
00:11:54,375 --> 00:11:57,250
We haven't seen any trails,
not even footprints.

306
00:11:58,833 --> 00:11:59,708
[disembodied whispering]

307
00:11:59,708 --> 00:12:02,541
Could the trees be whispering?

308
00:12:02,541 --> 00:12:04,750
[whispers swirling and growing]

309
00:12:04,750 --> 00:12:05,958
Follow the whispers!

310
00:12:07,916 --> 00:12:09,041
[Frak] ...and that's why

311
00:12:09,041 --> 00:12:11,250
we should obviously
head that way,

312
00:12:11,250 --> 00:12:13,291
toward those large,
pleasant trees.

313
00:12:13,291 --> 00:12:16,041
But I hear running water
over there.

314
00:12:16,041 --> 00:12:17,750
I'm sure it's clean
and refreshing,

315
00:12:17,750 --> 00:12:19,708
and unless you brought
a hose or a camel,

316
00:12:19,708 --> 00:12:21,250
we're going to need some.

317
00:12:21,250 --> 00:12:23,958
No, we need to get
to the Monastery of Ninjago,

318
00:12:23,958 --> 00:12:25,708
not to trees or water.

319
00:12:25,708 --> 00:12:27,708
As the most accomplished
Ninja here,

320
00:12:27,708 --> 00:12:28,708
I think we--

321
00:12:28,708 --> 00:12:30,458
Most accomplished Ninja?

322
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:33,750
Most accomplished at what,
being annoying?

323
00:12:33,750 --> 00:12:35,333
I'll be leading
this little group,

324
00:12:35,333 --> 00:12:36,583
thank you very much.

325
00:12:36,583 --> 00:12:39,000
[Wyldfyre chuckling]
Listen, before he died,

326
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:42,416
Egalt, one of the greatest
dragons to ever live,

327
00:12:42,416 --> 00:12:43,458
told me...
-[Riyu sniffing air]

328
00:12:43,458 --> 00:12:44,916
I'd be a leader someday.

329
00:12:44,916 --> 00:12:46,833
I'm thinking that day is today.

330
00:12:46,833 --> 00:12:48,083
No offense to Egalt,

331
00:12:48,083 --> 00:12:50,750
but even great masters
get things wrong sometimes.

332
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:52,375
[Frak] And that
doesn't change the fact

333
00:12:52,375 --> 00:12:54,333
that I was studying the Ninja

334
00:12:54,333 --> 00:12:56,708
before either of you
even heard of Spinjitzu.

335
00:12:56,708 --> 00:12:57,708
Really?

336
00:12:57,708 --> 00:12:59,916
Was that
when you were working for Ras?

337
00:12:59,916 --> 00:13:01,750
You worked for him
after I did.

338
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:03,666
[Sora] I was hanging with Arin.

339
00:13:03,666 --> 00:13:05,250
Ras just happened to be there.

340
00:13:05,250 --> 00:13:06,916
[Frak] You still did
what Ras said.

341
00:13:06,916 --> 00:13:07,916
[Sora groaning]

342
00:13:07,916 --> 00:13:09,541
[Cole] Hello?

343
00:13:09,541 --> 00:13:10,625
Anyone?

344
00:13:12,291 --> 00:13:13,708
The place is empty.

345
00:13:13,708 --> 00:13:14,750
Last I remember,

346
00:13:14,750 --> 00:13:16,916
something invisible attacked me,

347
00:13:16,916 --> 00:13:18,708
then I woke up here.

348
00:13:18,708 --> 00:13:20,416
You were in Spectral Sleep,

349
00:13:20,416 --> 00:13:22,250
and I was so focused
on trying to save you,

350
00:13:22,250 --> 00:13:23,916
I made some stupid mistakes

351
00:13:23,916 --> 00:13:25,333
and got my soul drained, too.

352
00:13:25,333 --> 00:13:28,666
I just hope Kai and the others
pulled through.

353
00:13:31,625 --> 00:13:32,708
[gasping]

354
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,083
Make sure you keep
her healing leaves warm

355
00:13:41,083 --> 00:13:42,750
with your hands.

356
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:45,416
That's how
my grandmother did it.

357
00:13:45,416 --> 00:13:47,875
Oh, no, what happened here?

358
00:13:47,875 --> 00:13:49,125
[Geo] Ras happened.

359
00:13:50,916 --> 00:13:51,750
Are you okay?

360
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:53,083
I'll be fine,

361
00:13:53,083 --> 00:13:55,416
but I don't know
about Rontu there.

362
00:13:55,416 --> 00:13:56,541
[groaning]

363
00:13:56,541 --> 00:13:59,041
What did Ras come here for?

364
00:13:59,041 --> 00:14:00,125
No clue.

365
00:14:00,125 --> 00:14:01,333
He forced me

366
00:14:01,333 --> 00:14:03,958
to take him
to Master Wu's old study,

367
00:14:03,958 --> 00:14:06,041
and I think he took something,

368
00:14:06,041 --> 00:14:08,500
but I don't know what,

369
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:10,041
or why.

370
00:14:10,041 --> 00:14:12,291
Then he left
through the Portal Gate.

371
00:14:12,291 --> 00:14:13,958
Whatever Ras is up to,

372
00:14:13,958 --> 00:14:16,208
it can't be good.

373
00:14:16,208 --> 00:14:18,416
It never is.

374
00:14:20,208 --> 00:14:22,041
[disembodied whispers swirling]

375
00:14:22,041 --> 00:14:23,583
Where is this taking us?

376
00:14:25,541 --> 00:14:26,875
[distant shrieking and roaring]

377
00:14:26,875 --> 00:14:28,083
That sounds bad.

378
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,083
[beings shrieking]

379
00:14:31,916 --> 00:14:33,041
[roaring]

380
00:14:33,041 --> 00:14:34,791
[shrieking]

381
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:37,500
[shrieking]

382
00:14:38,750 --> 00:14:40,333
[roaring]

383
00:14:44,958 --> 00:14:45,958
[roaring]

384
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:50,000
[Euphrasia gasping]
What are those things?

385
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:50,958
No idea,

386
00:14:50,958 --> 00:14:52,833
but you thinking
what I'm thinking?

387
00:14:52,833 --> 00:14:54,708
[Lloyd] Ninja... go!

388
00:15:04,750 --> 00:15:06,041
[smacking]

389
00:15:08,125 --> 00:15:08,958
[grunting with effort]

390
00:15:08,958 --> 00:15:10,750
Ugh, this is the worst!

391
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,625
[roaring]

392
00:15:12,625 --> 00:15:14,083
[Lloyd groaning]

393
00:15:16,666 --> 00:15:18,416
[Euphrasia straining,
wind gusting]

394
00:15:18,416 --> 00:15:19,416
[powers spluttering]

395
00:15:21,041 --> 00:15:22,500
Oh! Uh, sorry!

396
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:23,958
Accident!
[chuckling awkwardly]

397
00:15:23,958 --> 00:15:25,333
I'm usually better at that!

398
00:15:25,333 --> 00:15:27,041
[Arin] These are the weirdest
Elemental Masters

399
00:15:27,041 --> 00:15:28,250
I've ever seen.

400
00:15:28,250 --> 00:15:30,416
[Lloyd] I don't think
they're masters.

401
00:15:30,416 --> 00:15:33,083
I think they're actually
made of Elemental Powers.

402
00:15:33,083 --> 00:15:34,666
[snapping claws]

403
00:15:34,666 --> 00:15:35,791
[Arin] What?

404
00:15:35,791 --> 00:15:37,375
How is that even possible?

405
00:15:37,375 --> 00:15:38,666
[Lloyd] Don't ask me.

406
00:15:38,666 --> 00:15:40,791
Wu didn't prepare me
for anything like this!

407
00:15:44,916 --> 00:15:46,458
[roaring]

408
00:15:46,666 --> 00:15:48,375
Oh! Uh...

409
00:15:48,375 --> 00:15:51,625
Never used one of these before,
but, uh...

410
00:15:57,750 --> 00:15:59,916
[acid hissing]

411
00:15:59,916 --> 00:16:01,875
[roaring]

412
00:16:01,875 --> 00:16:02,833
Uh-oh.

413
00:16:05,541 --> 00:16:06,458
H'ah!

414
00:16:11,333 --> 00:16:12,208
[roaring]

415
00:16:13,208 --> 00:16:14,083
Ah!

416
00:16:19,833 --> 00:16:21,458
[Arin] Get to safety!

417
00:16:24,083 --> 00:16:26,208
[grunting with effort] H'yah!

418
00:16:26,875 --> 00:16:29,208
[acid hissing]

419
00:16:29,208 --> 00:16:30,666
[monster screeching]

420
00:16:30,666 --> 00:16:31,875
[Lloyd struggling]

421
00:16:34,583 --> 00:16:36,833
[Lloyd] No!

422
00:16:36,833 --> 00:16:38,750
[disembodied whispering]

423
00:16:38,750 --> 00:16:40,375
What the...?

424
00:16:42,375 --> 00:16:44,750
[whispers swirling]

425
00:16:52,333 --> 00:16:54,041
[bursting and sparking]

426
00:16:59,416 --> 00:17:00,333
[♪♪♪]

427
00:17:00,333 --> 00:17:02,041
H'yah!

428
00:17:02,041 --> 00:17:04,083
H'ah! H'yah!

429
00:17:05,833 --> 00:17:06,833
[♪♪♪]

430
00:17:06,833 --> 00:17:08,708
[Arin]
Lloyd got his powers working?

431
00:17:08,708 --> 00:17:10,416
[gasping] I'm back too!

432
00:17:12,708 --> 00:17:13,750
[♪♪♪]

433
00:17:20,416 --> 00:17:22,750
[monster groaning]

434
00:17:23,916 --> 00:17:26,000
[sparking and crackling]

435
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:29,083
Uh... did we... destroy them?

436
00:17:29,083 --> 00:17:31,166
[sighing] Not sure.

437
00:17:31,166 --> 00:17:33,083
If they're pure Elemental power,

438
00:17:33,083 --> 00:17:35,791
they may have just...
changed to another form.

439
00:17:36,583 --> 00:17:37,541
[sparking and spluttering]

440
00:17:37,541 --> 00:17:39,375
Aw, no!

441
00:17:39,375 --> 00:17:40,208
[groaning] Come on.

442
00:17:40,208 --> 00:17:42,541
[sighing] Too good to last.

443
00:17:42,541 --> 00:17:43,375
Can I just say,

444
00:17:43,375 --> 00:17:45,083
this place might be beautiful,

445
00:17:45,083 --> 00:17:47,250
but it is weird!

446
00:17:47,250 --> 00:17:48,500
[beings chittering
and squeaking]

447
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:50,666
[Euphrasia laughing]

448
00:17:50,666 --> 00:17:52,833
Guess they're happy
we saved them?

449
00:17:53,916 --> 00:17:56,291
[chittering]

450
00:17:56,291 --> 00:17:57,708
[Arin] Follow them?

451
00:17:57,708 --> 00:17:59,625
Don't have any better ideas.

452
00:17:59,625 --> 00:18:02,125
[beings chittering]

453
00:18:02,125 --> 00:18:03,416
Weird, but cute.

454
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:06,041
[wind gusting]

455
00:18:06,041 --> 00:18:07,625
[Riyu sniffing and snuffling]

456
00:18:07,625 --> 00:18:09,916
[grumbling and sniffing]

457
00:18:09,916 --> 00:18:11,708
Another reason
I should be the leader?

458
00:18:11,708 --> 00:18:12,833
If it wasn't for me,

459
00:18:12,833 --> 00:18:14,708
we'd still be fighting that...

460
00:18:14,708 --> 00:18:16,000
[nervously] ...puppet
in the desert.

461
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,500
You stop one puppet,

462
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:19,083
and you think
that makes you our leader?

463
00:18:19,083 --> 00:18:21,291
It was a big puppet!

464
00:18:21,291 --> 00:18:24,583
Man, all this walking
has made me thirsty.

465
00:18:24,583 --> 00:18:26,291
Then you should've listened
when I suggested

466
00:18:26,291 --> 00:18:28,208
we follow the sound
of running water!

467
00:18:28,208 --> 00:18:29,875
Looks like we don't need to.

468
00:18:29,875 --> 00:18:32,125
[Sora] How did we
not see that before?

469
00:18:33,666 --> 00:18:36,000
Who cares? [sighing]

470
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,666
You're right about one thing,

471
00:18:37,666 --> 00:18:39,416
all this walking...

472
00:18:39,416 --> 00:18:40,416
[slurping]

473
00:18:40,416 --> 00:18:42,375
...I could use a rest.

474
00:18:42,375 --> 00:18:44,125
Hmm, perfect!

475
00:18:44,125 --> 00:18:45,375
What are the chances?

476
00:18:47,333 --> 00:18:49,083
[stomach growling]

477
00:18:49,083 --> 00:18:51,083
Oh, wish we brought some food.

478
00:18:51,083 --> 00:18:54,250
I could use a Wyldmelon
right about now.

479
00:19:05,916 --> 00:19:07,833
[Arin] Okay,
so, thinking this through,

480
00:19:07,833 --> 00:19:10,958
both of your Elemental Powers
are acting strange,
`
481
01:19:10,958 --> 01:19:12,500
the Portal Gates aren't working,

481
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:15,833
and monsters that look like
pure Elemental Energy show up.

482
00:19:15,833 --> 00:19:18,375
[Euphrasia]
You think it's all related?

483
00:19:18,375 --> 00:19:20,083
It's a good question,

484
00:19:20,083 --> 00:19:22,750
and how did these trees
give me my powers back,

485
00:19:22,750 --> 00:19:24,666
at least for a little while?

486
00:19:24,666 --> 00:19:26,833
I didn't get a tree blast
like you did,

487
00:19:26,833 --> 00:19:28,916
but mine still came back.

488
00:19:28,916 --> 00:19:31,750
[Lloyd] I hope these little guys
are leading us to some answers.

489
00:19:33,708 --> 00:19:36,250
[deep rumbling]

490
00:19:36,250 --> 00:19:37,791
[♪♪♪]

491
00:19:37,791 --> 00:19:40,583
[groaning]

492
00:19:42,958 --> 00:19:44,916
[heaving and rumbling]

493
00:19:44,916 --> 00:19:46,041
[beings chittering]

494
00:19:46,041 --> 00:19:47,583
[gasping in awe] Wow...

495
00:19:52,291 --> 00:19:54,125
[disembodied whispering,
wind gusting]

496
00:19:54,125 --> 00:19:55,875
Whoa...

497
00:19:55,875 --> 00:19:57,916
Is that a Source Dragon?

498
00:19:57,916 --> 00:20:02,083
I... don't think so?

499
00:20:06,791 --> 00:20:08,625
[rumbling and stretching]

500
00:20:08,625 --> 00:20:10,583
[Arin quietly]
Are we supposed to say hi?

501
00:20:10,583 --> 00:20:12,208
Greetings, mighty dragon.

502
00:20:12,208 --> 00:20:13,500
My name is--

503
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:14,708
<i>[Arc Dragon, telepathically]</i>
<i>I know who you are,</i>

504
00:20:14,708 --> 00:20:16,750
<i>Lloyd, Son of Garmadon.</i>

505
00:20:16,750 --> 00:20:19,166
<i>My trees sensed</i>
<i>the Elemental Master of Life</i>

506
00:20:19,166 --> 00:20:21,041
<i>the moment you arrived</i>
<i>in our wood,</i>

507
00:20:21,041 --> 00:20:23,583
<i>and sent their whispers to me.</i>

508
00:20:25,750 --> 00:20:29,250
<i>We had long given up</i>
<i>on the Legendary Green Ninja</i>

509
00:20:29,250 --> 00:20:30,916
<i>ever returning to us.</i>

510
00:20:30,916 --> 00:20:32,250
Returned?

511
00:20:32,250 --> 00:20:33,541
<i>[annoyed] For generations,</i>

512
00:20:33,541 --> 00:20:35,000
<i>the Protector</i>
<i>of the Whispering Wood</i>

513
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,625
<i>has performed their duties,</i>

514
00:20:36,625 --> 00:20:40,875
<i>but you are the first</i>
<i>who ignored those duties,</i>

515
00:20:40,875 --> 00:20:43,500
<i>and we have long felt betrayed.</i>

516
00:20:44,625 --> 00:20:46,666
What...?

517
00:20:46,666 --> 00:20:48,750
[roaring mightily]

518
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:52,041
[Chief Loyalist] ...and so,
all I've hypothesized

519
00:20:52,041 --> 00:20:53,250
has been proven.

520
00:20:53,250 --> 00:20:54,708
Without realizing it,

521
00:20:54,708 --> 00:20:57,250
our enemies have
inadvertently set in motion

522
00:20:57,250 --> 00:20:59,000
their own downfall,

523
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,000
and our restoration.

524
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:04,083
The energy manifestations
have already begun.

525
00:21:04,083 --> 00:21:05,416
[Loyalists applauding]

526
00:21:05,416 --> 00:21:07,833
[Loyalist #1]
Ha! A triumph!

527
00:21:07,833 --> 00:21:09,041
[Loyalist #2]
But these creatures,

528
00:21:09,041 --> 00:21:10,250
what do they want?

529
00:21:10,250 --> 00:21:12,083
[Chief Loyalist] Want?
Why, nothing.

530
00:21:12,083 --> 00:21:14,291
They are beings of rage
and destruction

531
00:21:14,291 --> 00:21:16,958
born from the imbalance
of Source Energy,

532
00:21:16,958 --> 00:21:19,291
as manifested by the Weapon.

533
00:21:19,291 --> 00:21:21,583
If we backtrace a manifestation,

534
00:21:21,583 --> 00:21:23,583
we'll find the origin point,

535
00:21:23,583 --> 00:21:27,166
the location
of the Weapon of Desolation.

536
00:21:27,166 --> 00:21:29,583
[Loyalists applauding
and laughing] Well done! Yes!

537
00:21:29,583 --> 00:21:30,583
[Chief Loyalist] Now, go.

538
00:21:30,583 --> 00:21:32,291
Search your assigned regions!

539
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:33,333
Find the Weapon!

540
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:35,166
Let nothing stand in your way!

541
00:21:38,250 --> 00:21:41,583
Her time
will finally come again.

542
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,916
[♪♪♪]

